 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the directory's inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic therefore publishes every specialty it knows, under its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` (stated by the owner 2026-08-17). A veterinarian is shown by full name — first name, then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere here, because the page lists specialties rather than the roster. Every specialty is on one page, with no paging. The page offers no search over specialties and changes no record. It is reached by opening its own address: nothing links to it, and it carries the navigation every page carries without adding an entry for itself. Its own labels follow the language rules that bind every page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the page is opened, then every veterinarian holding it is listed by first name and last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the page is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given more specialties than one screen holds, when the page is opened, then all of them are present and no paging control is offered.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the supported languages, when the page's own labels are checked, then no wording is hard-coded and every label is present in each language.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty held by no veterinarian is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. A veterinarian holding several specialties is listed under each of them.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
